---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import ChecklistCta from '../components/ChecklistCta.astro';
import { PACKAGES as packages, SERVICES as services, OFFERINGS } from '../data/services.js';
---
<Base title="Services" description="PHP and Laravel security audits, WordPress malware cleanup, application upgrades, monitoring, and consultation for sites you are authorized to manage. Contact for quote.">
<div class="page-prose">
<h1>Services</h1>
<p>Hands-on help for PHP, Laravel and WordPress sites. All work is done only for sites you own or are authorized to manage (see our <a href="/authorized-work">authorized-work policy</a>).</p>
<!-- TODO(Raghav): add pricing or "starting from" details for each service. Intentionally left blank. -->
<p class="notice"><strong>Pricing:</strong> Contact for quote. Every site is different, so the price is agreed in writing after a short scoping chat. <a href="/contact">Request a quote</a>.</p>
<section id="packages" aria-labelledby="pk-title">
<h2 id="pk-title">Fixed-scope audit packages</h2>
<p>Clear scope, clear deliverables, agreed in writing before work starts. Turnaround counts business days from when access is confirmed.</p>
{packages.map(p => <article class="card">
  <h3>{p.name}</h3><p>{p.for}</p>
  <h4>Deliverables</h4><ul>{p.deliverables.map(d => <li>{d}</li>)}</ul>
  <p><strong>Turnaround:</strong> {p.turnaround}</p>
  <p><strong>Price:</strong> Contact for quote. <a class="btn primary" href="/contact">Request the {p.name}</a></p>
</article>)}
<p><small>Out of scope for all packages unless agreed in writing: fixing the findings, load/DoS testing, social engineering, and any system you are not authorized to test.</small></p>
</section>
<nav aria-label="Services"><ul>{services.map(s => <li><a href={`#${s.id}`}>{s.title}</a></li>)}</ul></nav>
{services.map(s => <section id={s.id}>
  <h2>{s.title}</h2><p>{s.intro}</p>
  <h3>What's included</h3><ul>{s.included.map(x => <li>{x}</li>)}</ul>
  <h3>Process</h3><ol>{s.process.map(x => <li>{x}</li>)}</ol>
  <p><strong>Price:</strong> {s.price}</p>
  <p><a class="btn primary" href="/contact">Ask about {s.title.toLowerCase()}</a></p>
</section>)}
<section id="focus" aria-labelledby="focus-title">
<h2 id="focus-title">More specific work</h2>
<p>These sit alongside the packages and services above. Scope is agreed in writing before any access or change. The price for each one is contact for quote.</p>
{OFFERINGS.map((item) => <section id={item.id}>
  <h3>{item.title}</h3>
  <p>{item.intro}</p>
  <h4>What's included</h4>
  <ul>{item.included.map((line) => <li>{line}</li>)}</ul>
  <p><strong>Price:</strong> {item.price}. <a href="/contact">Request a quote</a>.</p>
</section>)}
</section>
<ChecklistCta />
<section aria-labelledby="outline-title">
<h2 id="outline-title">Example report outline</h2>
<p><strong>This is an example of structure, not a client report.</strong> It does not describe a real site, a real finding, or a completed engagement.</p>
<ol>
<li>Scope and who authorized the work</li>
<li>Versions and components that were actually reviewed</li>
<li>Findings, each with severity, where it was seen, and a fix step</li>
<li>What was not tested</li>
<li>A suggested order for fixes</li>
</ol>
</section>
<section aria-labelledby="next-step"><h2 id="next-step">Next step</h2><p>Tell us about your site and the issue on the <a href="/contact">contact page</a>. We reply by email to agree scope, access and a quote before any work starts.</p><p><a class="btn primary" href="/contact">Request an audit or cleanup</a></p></section>
</div></Base>
